    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d545">

                <pb facs="0895" n="879" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg879"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/9–451</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of Defense</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marshall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-04">September 4,
                        1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Department of Defense
                    has considered your department’s Draft Position Paper (WFM–T–10/1) dated <pb
                        facs="0896" n="880" xml:id="pg880"/> 18 August 1951, and entitled “United
                    Nations Action in Korea in Case of No Armistice”.</p>
                <p>The Department of Defense is unable to concur in this paper for the reasons set
                    forth in the enclosed memoranda from the Joint Chiefs of Staff, dated 29 August
                    1951, and 13 July 1951.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d545-f1"/> I am in agreement with
                    the comments and recommendations of the Joint Chiefs of Staff as set forth in
                    these two memoranda with the exception of the recommendation in paragraph 1-<hi
                        rendition="#italic">e</hi> of the memorandum of 13 July.</p>
                <p>Because of the important implications involved in this particular recommendation,
                    I am reserving my position with respect to it and am transmitting the views of
                    the Joint Chiefs of Staff to the National Security Council for early
                        consideration.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d545-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d545-a1.xml" xpointer="d545-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
